# demo-video transcript template — the Claude turn `claude-intake.cast` appends (Issue #2833)
#
# One Claude Code session turn in the JSONL dialect
# src/lib/hooks/sources/claude/transcript.ts reads, shaped like
# claude-delegate.jsonl: the operator's prompt (`origin.kind: human`,
# `promptSource: typed` — the markers #2196 requires before a `user` row is
# written), TWO tool rounds, and the closing assistant record
# (`stop_reason: end_turn` with prose — what #2264 requires before the turn may
# be written). fake-agent.sh's `@transcript` row appends every non-comment line
# to the file named by --transcript, replacing {{NOW}} {{TURN}} {{SESSION_ID}}
# {{CWD}} {{WORKTREE}} {{MESSAGE}} {{EXEC_OUTPUT}} at replay time.
#
# Two rounds rather than one, because they are the beat the cut is about: the
# half-formed thought the phone sent becomes a task contract FIRST (`Write`,
# the `.commandmate/tasks/*.yaml` shape the contract reader parses), and only
# then is handed to a second agent (`Bash`, the `commandmate ask … --instance
# codex` the cassette's `@exec` really runs). The chat surface draws them as
# the trailing tool-activity section (#2234), which the scene opens by seeding
# `commandmate:chatShowToolActivity`.
#
# The last record's text is the Markdown the chat surface renders; the
# `[Header.tsx](src/components/layout/Header.tsx)` link is what becomes a
# ChatFileLink (#2345), and the phone taps it. What the link says about the
# file is what the file says: the seed's Header.tsx carries
# `aria-label="Toggle dark mode"` on the toggle. No personal path: `cwd` is the
# seed worktree.
